{"resultsPerPage":3,"startIndex":0,"totalResults":3,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T11:05:22.920","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-113630","sourceIdentifier":"cve@rapid7.com","published":"2026-11-16T17:17:29.080","lastModified":"2026-11-16T21:17:20.297","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Command injection in the documentserver-flush-cache.sh maintenance helper in ONLYOFFICE Docs (Document Server) 9.4.0-129 on the official onlyoffice/documentserver container allows a local attacker with command execution as the ds user to execute arbitrary commands as root via a crafted --hash argument that is interpolated unvalidated into a GNU sed expression, where the sed e flag runs attacker-controlled commands. The packaged sudoers policy permits ds to run the helper as root without a password and with unrestricted arguments."}],"affected":[{"source":"cve@rapid7.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"ONLYOFFICE","product":"Docs (Document Server)","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":[{"version":"9.4.0-129","lessThan":"10.0.0","versionType":"semver","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"cve@rapid7.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"LOCAL","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":1.8,"impactScore":5.9}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:34:25.508842Z","id":"CVE-2026-113630","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"cve@rapid7.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-78"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/jburgess-r7/onlyoffice-2026-pocs","source":"cve@rapid7.com"},{"url":"https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-from-view-only-access-to-container-root-five-vulnerabilities-in-onlyoffice-docs-fixed/","source":"cve@rapid7.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-131800","sourceIdentifier":"product-cna@github.com","published":"2026-11-18T03:17:41.450","lastModified":"2026-11-18T20:19:08.677","vulnStatus":"Received","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"A stored cross-site scripting vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that allowed an organization member with permission to manage custom-property definitions and edit property values to add an attacker-controlled SSH authentication key to the personal account of another member through HTML stored in a single-select custom-property option. Exploitation required another definition manager in the same organization to attempt to remove the poisoned option while it was in use and save the definition with a valid sudo session. Repository access through the added key depended on the permissions of the victim and independent authorization controls. This vulnerability affected supported GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 3.23 and was fixed in versions 3.19.16, 3.20.12, 3.21.10, and 3.22.5. This vulnerability was reported via the GitHub Bug Bounty program."}],"affected":[{"source":"product-cna@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"GitHub","product":"Enterprise Server","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":[{"version":"3.19.0","lessThan":"3.19.*","versionType":"semver","status":"affected","changes":[{"at":"3.19.16","status":"unaffected"}]},{"version":"3.20.0","lessThan":"3.20.*","versionType":"semver","status":"affected","changes":[{"at":"3.20.12","status":"unaffected"}]},{"version":"3.21.0","lessThan":"3.21.*","versionType":"semver","status":"affected","changes":[{"at":"3.21.10","status":"unaffected"}]},{"version":"3.22.0","lessThan":"3.22.*","versionType":"semver","status":"affecte